-- §2  The compositions: every splice site, and the template it lands in.
# One row per (parent, child) edge of the compose graph, with how many times the parent splices
# the child. Every splice site and the child it lands in, handed over whole.
#
# The other three readings are taken in Rust
#   How many sites land in each template, which parents compose the same set of children, and how
#   those counts are spread are each one `GROUP BY` away from here. Writing them as three more
#   templates would be the queries describing themselves in their own terms, so
#   `examples/combinatorics` works them out from the edge list by a route that shares no SQL with
#   rank/.
#
# The zeros come from the directory
#   A template nothing composes has no edge, so no count grouped from this relation can show it:
#   `GROUP BY` lists only what some row reached. The program drives from `assets/sqlc/` on disk to
#   see them, as the `unreached` check in `examples/observations` does.
-- rank/compose_edges.sqlc, the edge list as it stands.
SELECT e.parent AS "parent!", e.child AS "child!", e.splices::bigint AS "splices!"
FROM (
    :compose(rank/compose_edges.sqlc)
) e
ORDER BY e.parent, e.child
